Experimental source-owned startup logging; not automatically applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006 bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires prior caller/auth/refusal/restricted/catalog/settings/empty-auth/presence/telemetry/marketplace patches.
Modules: utils/logger::{ownStartupLogging,retireStartupLogging,setTransports,registerLogSink,setLogForwarder,schedulePruneStaleProcessLogs}; CLI and sdk exact-session binding.
Tests: startup-logging-owner.test.ts, startup-logging-cli.test.ts, existing logger, SDK and CLI suites.
Difference: --startup-no-logging requires --restrict-tools and owns the local logger;
it closes original transport, joins queued original retention callbacks and blocks
late transport, sink and forwarder changes. Ordinary logging remains available
without the flag. Other logging implementations, complete inventory, Ready, paid
execution, signing and release acceptance remain open.

